{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said, etc., he will not obey.</b> The intention here is perhaps that Moses thought that when Pharaoh sees all the signs and wonders that Moses had performed, even though he sees that Israel has departed and not returned — perhaps terror and dread will fall upon him and he will not pursue the children of Israel. Therefore He informed him: ״he will not obey״ — meaning, he will not accept [it] from you — meaning, with regard to what you think, that he has resolved his mind concerning Israel. And He spoke in the future tense: even after the plague of the firstborn I will not humble his heart to the ultimate degree to agree to send them forth with finality. And the reason is ״in order to multiply My signs in the land of Egypt״ — when he pursues after them. And His saying ״land״ — they of blessed memory already said (Mekhilta, parsha 14) concerning the verse ״for HaShem fights for them in Egypt״, etc.; see his words there." "<b>Further,</b> it intends: since Moses said <b>and they shall bow down to me, saying: Go out, you and all the people who are at your feet</b>, and the meaning of ״at your feet״ is בִּרְשׁוּתְךָ (in your domain) — behold, he took the people out of Pharaoh's domain and placed them in the domain of Moses our shepherd, our king, and by this he revealed to him that their departure from Egypt was through the uprooting of Pharaoh's dominion from over them. Therefore HaShem said to him <b>Pharaoh will not obey you</b> — meaning, Pharaoh will not comprehend your words. And the reason: ״in order to multiply My signs״ — for if he comprehends the matter from the time he says to you at night (Exodus 12:31) ״arise, go out״, he will firmly establish the matter and will have no reason to pursue them afterward, and there will be no place for the signs that I wish to multiply — two hundred and fifty plagues that shall surround him."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:47.895690580Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}